{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "לישראל במראות הלילה", :translit "le-yisra'el be-mar'ot ha-laylah", :gloss "to Israel in visions of the night"} {:he "ז' תגין סשי״ן", :translit "zayin tagin shin", :gloss "seven tagin [on the] shin"} {:he "כי שבע יפול צדיק וקם", :translit "ki sheva yipol tzadik v'kam", :gloss "for seven times a righteous man falls and rises"} {:he "עשו לבן מלאך דינה יוסף שמעון בנימין", :translit "esav lavan mal'ach dinah yosef shim'on binyamin", :gloss "Esau, Laban, angel, Dinah, Joseph, Simeon, Benjamin"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Seven tagin are written on the ש of לישראל corresponding to seven troubles from which Jacob was delivered."}], :frame {:text "Proverbs 24:16 states 'for a righteous man falls seven times and rises.' The verse in Genesis 46:2 reads לישראל, and the letter ש is decorated with seven tagin to signal that Jacob (= ישראל, Genesis 35:10) endured seven crises and survived each. The list of seven is: Esau (Genesis 27:41), Laban (Genesis 31:36–42), the angel (Genesis 32:25–31), Dinah (Genesis 34:1–5), Joseph's disappearance (Genesis 37:33–35), Simeon's detention in Egypt (Genesis 42:24, 36), and the threat to Benjamin in Egypt (Genesis 43:1–14, 44:18–34).", :sources ["Proverbs 24:16" "Genesis 46:2" "Genesis 35:10" "Genesis 27:41" "Genesis 31:36–42" "Genesis 32:25–31" "Genesis 34:1–5" "Genesis 37:33–35" "Genesis 42:24" "Genesis 42:36" "Genesis 43:1–14" "Genesis 44:18–34"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Seven tagin are written on the ש of לישראל corresponding to seven troubles from which Jacob was delivered.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 46, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:11:47.877322333Z", :model "glm-5.2"}